<%# Row metadata on a record page (docs/design/design.md, "Record pages"): when the row was added and
    last updated, and its ID, as one quiet line under the content. They describe the database row,
    not the record, so they don't get a card of their own (decisions.md, 2026-11-27).
    Locals: record; added_label ("Added" unless given, e.g. "Provisioned"); with_time (false unless
    given: users and beacons show the time of day, because sign-ups and syncs happen within a day). %>
<% added_label = local_assigns.fetch(:added_label, "Added") %>
<% format = local_assigns.fetch(:with_time, false) ? "%b %-d, %Y at %-l:%M %p" : "%b %-d, %Y" %>
<p class="record-meta">
  <span><%= added_label %> <time datetime="<%= record.created_at.iso8601 %>"><%= record.created_at.strftime(format) %></time></span>
  <span>Last updated <time datetime="<%= record.updated_at.iso8601 %>"><%= record.updated_at.strftime(format) %></time></span>
  <span>ID <b><%= record.id %></b></span>
</p>
